Application availability testing helps organizations verify that applications remain accessible and responsive from expected locations. Monitoring availability is especially important for customer-facing applications.

Availability testing can help identify:

* Application downtime
* Slow responses
* Connectivity problems
* Regional availability issues
* Unexpected application failures

For example, a company operating an online shopping website can test the availability of its application and receive alerts when the site becomes inaccessible.

A real-life use case is a global organization monitoring a public application to determine whether customers in different geographic locations can access the service successfully.

Availability monitoring provides proactive visibility into user-facing service health.
